    "problem_statement": "CoAP clients mishandle separate responses. An empty acknowledgment of a confirmable request must stop retransmission while keeping the request pending for its later response or timeout. A response from the original endpoint with the original token must complete the request even when its message ID differs. Confirmable responses require an empty acknowledgment with the response message ID. Deliver response payloads intact even when sending a DTLS acknowledgment reuses receive storage. Responses with a different token or endpoint must not complete a pending request. Preserve ordinary piggybacked responses, retries and timeouts for unacknowledged requests, callback lifecycle, and unrelated-response behavior.",
    "platform": "native",
